me><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(617) 292-5500</voiceNum></cntPhone><cntAddress addressType="both"><delPoint>100 Cambridge Street - Suite 900</delPoint><city>Boston</city><adminArea>MA</adminArea><postCode>02114</postCode><country>US</country><eMailAdd>baw.edep@mass.gov</eMailAdd></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role><displayName>Tara Manno Richer</displayName><displayName>Tara Manno Richer</displayName></citRespParty></idCitation><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;The Massachusetts Department of Environmental Protection (MassDEP) Major Facilities data layer is a statewide point layer containing the location of a subset of facility types regulated by MassDEP’s Bureau of Air and Waste (Formerly the Bureau of Waste Prevention (BWP)).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;This layer contains the following major facility types: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;UL&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Facilities with Air Operating Permits (AIR) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Hazardous Waste Recyclers (HWR) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Hazardous Waste Treatment, Storage and/or Disposal Facilities (TSDF) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Large Quantity Generators of MA-regulated Hazardous Waste (LQG_MA) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Large Quantity Generators of EPA/RCRA-regulated Hazardous Waste (LQG_RCRA) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Large Quantity Toxic Users (LQTU) &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;The layer is stored and distributed as BWPMAJOR_PT&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Data Universe: &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;MassDEP’s Facility Master File Database (FMF)/Site Management System (SMS) database was queried to identify facilities engaging in the activities listed above. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Methods and sources used for facility location include the following:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;UL&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Site-specific knowledge of BAW Compliance and Enforcement staff &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;GPS field verification by MassDEP staff &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Surveys, site plans and locus maps from MassDEP records &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Interpolation of orthophoto imagery and parcel data from MassGIS &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Geocoding of FMF/SMS addresses using MassGIS Master Address Database (MAD)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;See related:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;UL&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Location Documentation Table (BWPMAJOR_PT_LDT) for documentation re: the types of features mapped, methods and sources used.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;Unlocated Sites List (BWPMAJOR_PT_USL) table for list of MassDEP Major Facilities that are unlocated and not included in this layer.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;P /&gt;&lt;P STYLE="margin:0 0 0 0;"&gt;&lt;SPAN /&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><idPurp>The Massachusetts Department of Environmental Protection (MassDEP) Major Facilities data layer is a statewide point layer containing the location of a subset of facility types regulated by MassDEP’s Bureau of Air and Waste (BAW).</idPurp><idStatus><ProgCd value="001"/></idStatus><resMaint xmlns=""><maintFreq><MaintFreqCd value="009"/></maintFreq></resMaint><themeKeys xmlns=""><keyword>Treatment Storage Disposal</keyword><keyword>LQG</keyword><keyword>Hazardous Waste</keyword><keyword>BWP</keyword><keyword>Bureau of Waste Prevention</keyword><keyword>RCRA</keyword><keyword>MassDEP</keyword><keyword>DEP</keyword><keyword>LQG-RCRA</keyword><keyword>HWR</keyword><keyword>GWD</keyword><keyword>SWD</keyword><keyword>HW</keyword><keyword>Toxics User</keyword><keyword>Surface Water Discharge</keyword><keyword>Surfacewater Discharge</keyword><keyword>Major Facilities</keyword><keyword>Large Quantity Generator</keyword><keyword>Ground Water Discharge</keyword><keyword>Groundwater Discharge</keyword><keyword>TSDF</keyword><keyword>LQTU</keyword><keyword>LQG-MA</keyword><keyword>Air Operating Permit</keyword><keyword>AIR</keyword><keyword>Air</keyword><keyword>Recycler</keyword><keyword>Toxic User</keyword></themeKeys><searchKeys><keyword>Treatment Storage Disposal</keyword><keyword>LQG</keyword><keyword>Hazardous Waste</keyword><keyword>BWP</keyword><keyword>Bureau of Waste Prevention</keyword><keyword>RCRA</keyword><keyword>MassDEP</keyword><keyword>DEP</keyword><keyword>LQG-RCRA</keyword><keyword>HWR</keyword><keyword>HW</keyword><keyword>Toxics User</keyword><keyword>Major Facilities</keyword><keyword>Large Quantity Generator</keyword><keyword>TSDF</keyword><keyword>LQTU</keyword><keyword>LQG-MA</keyword><keyword>Air Operating Permit</keyword><keyword>AIR</keyword><keyword>Air</keyword><keyword>Recycler</keyword><keyword>Toxic User</keyword></searchKeys><dataLang><languageCode value="eng"/><countryCode value="USA" Sync="TRUE"/></dataLang><dataExt xmlns=""><exDesc>publication date</exDesc></dataExt><envirDesc Sync="TRUE"> Version 6.2 (Build 9200) ; Esri ArcGIS 10.9.1.28388</envirDesc><spatRpType><SpatRepTypCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"/></spatRpType><dataExt xmlns=""><geoEle xmlns=""><GeoBndBox esriExtentType="search"><exTypeCode Sync="TRUE">1</exTypeCode><westBL Sync="TRUE">-73.347202</westBL><eastBL Sync="TRUE">-69.939535</eastBL><northBL Sync="TRUE">42.860769</northBL><southBL Sync="TRUE">41.251013</southBL></GeoBndBox></geoEle></dataExt><dataChar><CharSetCd value="004"/></dataChar><idCredit>MassDEP Bureau of Air and Waste (BAW)</idCredit><idPoC xmlns=""><rpOrgName>MassDEP Bureau of Air and Waste (BAW)</rpOrgName><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(617) 292-5500</voiceNum></cntPhone><cntAddress addressType="both"><delPoint>100 Cambridge Street - Suite 900</delPoint><city>Boston</city><adminArea>MA</adminArea><postCode>02114</postCode><country>US</country><eMailAdd>baw.edep@mass.gov</eMailAdd></cntAddress></rpCntInfo><role><RoleCd value="006"/></role><displayName>MassDEP Bureau of Air and Waste (BAW)</displayName></idPoC><tpCat><TopicCatCd value="017"/></tpCat></dataIdInfo><dqInfo xmlns=""><dqScope><scpLvl><ScopeCd value="005"/></scpLvl></dqScope><dataLineage><statement>Major landmarks in the development of the layer are as follows:  
- The layer was first conceived in April 1998.  
- The first major design changes came in March 2005 when Surface Water Discharges and Large Quantity generators of MA-regulated hazardous waste were added to the layer.  Feature-level metadata were removed from the attribute table and included in a related "location documentation" table.  
- November 2009 was the first edition of the layer in which all "major" categories, with the exception of MA-regulated LQGs, were 100% located.  
- In December 2011, point features for solid waste facilities (including municipal solid waste combustion facilities) were made available via MassGIS, separate from the solid waste polygon layer.  Please note MSW combustion facilities are a subset of the Air Operating Permits included in this layer.
- In January 2013 many BWP Major locations were refined using imagery from multiple years of orthophotography, updated parcel data and a large field mapping initiative undertaken to confirm the locations of underground storage tanks.  These updated UST locations are available via MassGIS.
- As of April 29, 2016: 2,106 features include refined locations and updated classification information presented in the "major" fields: AIR, HWR, LQG_MA, LQG_RCRA, LQTU, TSDF. Currently 68% of Large Quantity Generators of MA Regulated Waste (LQG_MA) and 100% of the other "major" categories have been located. Ground and Surface Water discharges are no longer regulated within the Bureau of Air and Waste, the GWD and SWD fields remain (null) for structural consistency.
-In 2023 the following attribute fields (GWD, RTN, NPDES_ID, SWD, SW_ID) contained in the 2016 version of this data are no longer supported and have been removed from the attribute table structure. 
